  "assessments": [
    {
      "ranges": "parent333-353,440-457,495-574",
      "contract": "Existing ConnectionPeer owns each listener immediately. Lexical JoinSets own every accepted child. Drop abort of the listener destroys its set; no direct detached child remains. Watch close and actual listener accept errors propagate via ?. Completed child errors accumulate while acceptance remains available, preserving independent reference barriers."
    },
    {
      "ranges": "parent582-621",
      "contract": "Normal watch finish stops accepting, attempts finite drain, then abort/join fallback. Completed causes live outside timed futures, so expiry cannot erase previously joined errors. Only explicitly aborted cancellation JoinError is accepted in fallback; unrelated join/worker/I/O/TLS causes propagate. Listener timeout preserves its actual Elapsed with any stop failure."
    },
    {
      "ranges": "parent101-231,243-275",
      "contract": "Recoverable startup/operation/observation failures route all acquired fixtures to explicit cleanup. Successful clients are retained in result values through cleanup. Multiple failures preserve primary and independent cleanup objects. Panic/outer timeout still use abort-on-Drop and can interrupt explicit observation."
    },
    {
      "ranges": "parent356-374,383-429,460-492,624-657",
      "contract": "Poison no longer fabricates empty counts or an unrecorded response. Concrete io::Error with CredentialObserverPoisoned source is returned before response emission. HTTP 407 variants, origin Connection: close/ok body, relay and TLS handshake unchanged. Same outer 20-second deadline and literal context expose actual Elapsed."
    },
    {
      "ranges": "peer264-320",
      "contract": "Additive combined-cause control reaches actual authenticated GET/body/count2/1/1 and real completed partial CONNECT. Primary PermissionDenied is explicitly injected afterward at the actual caller finish seam; cleanup requires concrete UnexpectedEof. Useful simultaneous cause test, not a measured natural caller failure."
    }
